WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.360
An animal can use a meal only after food is broken into molecules small enough to

2
00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:09.360
cross the gut lining.

3
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:14.880
The gut breaks food down, absorbs nutrients, water and salts, and eliminates what is

4
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.700
left. Different regions do different jobs.

5
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:23.160
In humans, most digestion and nutrient absorption happen in the small intestine.

6
00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:29.320
Its folds, villi and microvilli multiply the surface where nutrients cross into the

7
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:30.320
body.

8
00:00:30.583 --> 00:00:34.903
Teeth grind food. The stomach mixes it with acid and enzymes.

9
00:00:35.743 --> 00:00:40.383
The pancreas sends digestive enzymes and bicarbonate into the small intestine.

10
00:00:41.423 --> 00:00:43.023
Bicarbonate neutralizes acid.

11
00:00:43.963 --> 00:00:47.883
Bile salts break fat drops into smaller droplets that lipase can reach.

12
00:00:48.723 --> 00:00:51.583
Enzymes split molecules; bile is not an enzyme.

13
00:00:52.543 --> 00:00:55.483
Most absorbed sugars and amino acids enter blood.

14
00:00:56.323 --> 00:00:58.423
Most absorbed fat leaves through lymph vessels.

15
00:00:58.423 --> 00:01:01.883
The large intestine absorbs water and salts.

16
00:01:02.917 --> 00:01:05.397
Gut designs differ with diet and ancestry.

17
00:01:06.337 --> 00:01:09.537
A cow ferments food before its acid-secreting stomach region.

18
00:01:10.337 --> 00:01:12.457
A horse ferments after the small intestine.

19
00:01:13.517 --> 00:01:15.817
Gut length alone is no simple guide to diet.

20
00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:18.200
Who breaks down the fiber?

21
00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:23.500
Microbes ferment cellulose and release short-chain fatty acids, which the host

22
00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:29.100
absorbs. Cows digest microbes that pass into the acid-secreting stomach compartment.

23
00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.880
Horses ferment in the cecum and colon.

24
00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:34.340
Rabbits ferment in the cecum too.

25
00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:39.680
They eat soft cecal pellets, sending microbes and their protein through the stomach

26
00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:42.500
and small intestine for digestion and absorption.

27
00:01:43.650 --> 00:01:45.990
Nerves and hormones coordinate the work.

28
00:01:46.910 --> 00:01:49.050
Gut-wall nerves run local reflexes.

29
00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:54.090
In Pavlov's dogs, eating triggered stomach juice even when food never reached the

30
00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:57.490
stomach. Cutting both vagus nerves stopped that response.

31
00:01:58.450 --> 00:02:00.770
This showed nervous control before food arrived.

32
00:02:01.783 --> 00:02:03.323
Hormones travel in blood.

33
00:02:04.303 --> 00:02:07.943
Food in the stomach brings out gastrin, which increases acid secretion.

34
00:02:09.083 --> 00:02:14.483
Acid entering the duodenum brings out secretin, which drives pancreatic bicarbonate

35
00:02:14.483 --> 00:02:20.743
secretion. Fats and proteins bring out CCK, which drives pancreatic enzyme release

36
00:02:20.743 --> 00:02:23.263
and gallbladder contraction to release bile.

37
00:02:24.217 --> 00:02:28.997
Finally, an essential nutrient must come from food because an animal cannot make

38
00:02:28.997 --> 00:02:31.077
enough. Requirements differ.

39
00:02:32.057 --> 00:02:37.557
Humans need dietary vitamin C. Cats need dietary taurine, which adult humans make.
